course: dictionary
lesson: 15415
title: Squiggle: a short wavy line
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A squiggle is a short line that wiggles or curls, often drawn quickly and a bit messily. Look at the words around it for clues. «Ravi drew a squiggle across the page to show the snake.» A snake moves in wavy lines, so a squiggle must be a wavy line. Check by swapping in "wavy line": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Squiggle can also be a doing word, a verb. «The worm squiggled out of the soil.» The worm is not drawing anything. It is wriggling and twisting about. The word endings show the forms: squiggle, squiggles, squiggled, squiggling.
explain: Squiggle is a friendly, informal word. «The cake had a squiggle of pink icing on top» means a small curly line of icing, not a whole pattern. Ask yourself what the squiggle is made of and how it looks, and the clues will tell you the meaning.
fact: A squiggle is a short wavy or curly line.
fact: A squiggle is often drawn quickly or messily.
fact: As a verb, to squiggle means to draw such lines, or to wriggle or twist about.
fact: In maths notes, a squiggle "~" can mean "about" or "approximately".
fact: Squiggle, squiggles, squiggled and squiggling are all forms of the same word.
exercise: «Ravi drew a squiggle across the page to show the snake.» What is a squiggle? | A sharp pencil | *A short wavy or curly line | A large square box | A loud noise
exercise: «The worm squiggled out of the soil.» What does squiggled mean here? | *Wriggled and twisted about | Shouted loudly | Drew a picture | Fell asleep
exercise: In some maths notes, the symbol ~ can mean which word? | Under | Never | Ready | *About
test: «The cake was decorated with a squiggle of pink icing.» What is a squiggle here? | *A small curly line of icing | A bowl of cream | A spoon for stirring | A cake shaped like a square
test: «Lily squiggled her name at the bottom of the card.» What does squiggled mean here? | *Wrote it in quick, messy wavy lines | Read it out loud | Painted it in gold | Folded the card
exam: Maya says, «My handwriting is all squiggles.» What does she mean? | She has written a very long story | Her writing is neat and printed in capitals | Her pencil has broken | *Her writing is full of quick, messy wavy marks
